            "thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Assume AC. On every finite-dimensional complex manifold M the holomorphic structure sheaf O_M is coherent: the relation sheaf of any finite tuple of local holomorphic sections is locally finitely generated. Coherent O_M-modules are closed under kernels, cokernels and finite extensions. For every coherent F, point x and finite integer l\u22650, there is a chart neighborhood W of x on which F has an exact partial free resolution O_W^{p_l}\u2192\u2026\u2192O_W^{p_0}\u2192F|_W\u21920 by finite ranks. Exactness at the leftmost term is not asserted. No global analytic free resolution is claimed.",
          "strategy": "Prove the Weierstrass-induction relation lemma with generators uniform on one neighborhood, following Demailly II3.19\u20133.20. Handle zero/unit tuple entries and coordinate changes. Prove the elementary coherent-kernel calculus and obtain each finite partial resolution by successive coherent kernels and finite shrinking. Stalk Noetherianity alone is insufficient.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "axiom_base": "ZF + full AC; record resolutions, countable shrinking/diagonal choices, Baire/Fr\u00e9chet arguments and supplier-inherited choice uses precisely. No physical premise.",
