            "thm-long-exact-sequence-sheaf-cohomology": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Assume AC. Let F be coherent analytic on a neighborhood of a point x in C^N. There is a coordinate polydisc W about x such that for every nonempty coordinate polydisc D\u2282W and every q>0, H^q(D,F|_D)=0. Scalar sheaf cohomology on such D is computed by its smooth Dolbeault resolution. One can choose W subordinate to a partial finite-rank free resolution of F of length exceeding 2N. The assertion is local in the supplied resolution neighborhood; no untwisted projective Cartan A/B or global Stein generation theorem is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Write scalar Dolbeault sheaf exactness from the local lemma and smooth-module acyclicity, then global scalar polydisc vanishing. Establish the ordinary sheaf cohomological-dimension bound H^j(D,G)=0 for j>2N for arbitrary abelian sheaves on a polydisc, by explicit finite-order refinements/paracompact \u010cech comparison, not by misusing a compact-support bound. Choose a partial free resolution longer than 2N on W; dimension shift along its coherent kernels on every D\u2282W. No global Cartan A/B.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "axiom_base": "ZF + full AC; record resolutions, countable shrinking/diagonal choices, Baire/Fr\u00e9chet arguments and supplier-inherited choice uses precisely. No physical premise.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Demailly",
                "url": "https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf",
                "locator": "IX \u00a74.B, (4.3)\u2013Lemma4.4, printed/PDF p.421; proof read. Adapt to polydiscs using actual scalar suppliers and a separately proved 2N ordinary cohomological-dimension bound."
              }
            ]
          },
          "proof_contract_plan": {
            "state": "unproved proposal; no local proof/native approval",
            "obligations": [
              "Write scalar Dolbeault sheaf exactness from the local lemma and smooth-module acyclicity, then global scalar polydisc vanishing",
              "Establish the ordinary sheaf cohomological-dimension bound H^j(D,G)=0 for j>2N for arbitrary abelian sheaves on a polydisc, by explicit finite-order refinements/paracompact \u010cech comparison, not by misusing a compact-support bound",
              "Choose a partial free resolution longer than 2N on W; dimension shift along its coherent kernels on every D\u2282W",
              "No global Cartan A/B."
