          "statement": "Assume AC. For 0\u2264r\u22643 and any coherent analytic O_{P^r(C)}-module F, every H^q(P^r(C),F), q\u22650, is finite-dimensional. With the locally defined coherent-section Fr\u00e9chet topology and the induced \u010cech quotient topology these cohomology groups are Hausdorff. The proof includes the required Fr\u00e9chet open-mapping and Schwartz compact-complex finiteness results, local coherent-section topology, and compactness of restriction; none is presumed to follow from a Banach-only or one-variable theorem.",
          "strategy": "Develop metrizable complete locally convex section spaces and prove the Fr\u00e9chet open-mapping theorem by Baire and successive approximation; Banach open mapping is only an analogy. Prove Schwartz compact-perturbation and its compact morphism of Fr\u00e9chet complexes finite-dimensional/Hausdorff cohomology corollary. Define coherent section topology as a closed-relation quotient and show chart/generator independence using Artin\u2013Rees/Krull. Prove several-variable Montel from polydisc Cauchy estimates, Ascoli and diagonal compact exhaustion (the imported named Montel theorem is plane-only). Prove compact coherent restriction maps. Construct finite nested Leray covers of P^r subordinate to distinguished resolution neighborhoods and justify all finite-intersection acyclicity. If intersections are not coordinate polydiscs, explicitly prove their pseudoconvex chart geometry and scalar Dolbeault vanishing, then coherent dimension shifting; do not apply pair3 to arbitrary intersections. Apply the proved compact-complex theorem to the resulting restriction of \u010cech complexes. This contains substantial internal prerequisites and remains unproved.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "axiom_base": "ZF + full AC; record resolutions, countable shrinking/diagonal choices, Baire/Fr\u00e9chet arguments and supplier-inherited choice uses precisely. No physical premise.",
