s":"mathematical-premise","thm-long-exact-tor-sequence-in-the-right-module-variable":"mathematical-premise"},"statement":"Assume AC. Let X be a finite-type complex scheme, x a complex closed point, and define X^an locally by extending a finite polynomial defining ideal to convergent holomorphic functions, retaining nilpotents. The canonical local map A=O_{X,x}→B=O_{X^an,x} is injective and faithfully flat; its induced map on maximal-ideal completions is an isomorphism. In Serre’s flat-pair convention, B/A is flat over A and M→M⊗_A B is injective for every A-module M. On an affine ambient chart at x, C[t]_(t) and C{t} have common completion C[[t]], and the quotient comparison is compatible with every finitely generated defining ideal. This is a local-ring assertion, not a relative direct-image theorem.","strategy":"Identify finite jets on polynomial local and convergent rings by truncation and finite degree-k monomial grouping of convergent tails. Apply existing completion flatness: T is flat over A and faithfully flat over B. For each injection of A-modules tensor its B-kernel with T, use A-flatness of T and faithful reflection to get zero kernel. Prove local faithfulness and unit injection, then Tor gives B/A flat. Pass to the same extended defining ideal for finite-type quotients; do not invoke reduced-set Nullstellensatz.","proof_strategy":"direct","axiom_base":"ZF + full AC; record resolutions, countable shrinking/diagonal choices, Baire/Fréchet arguments and supplier-inherited choice uses precisely. No physical premise.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-supplied"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Serre","url":"https://www.college-de-france.fr/media/jean-pierre-serre/UPL1698785858825941763_Serre_GAGA.pdf","locator":"§6 Proposition3/Corollary1 printed pp.9–11; Annex Propositions22–23,27–29 printed pp.36–40; read."}]},"proof_contract_plan":{"state":"unproved proposal; no local proof/native approval","obligations":["Identify finite jets