PLAN {"id":"qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing-on-the-round-four-sphere","title":"Coupled Penrose vanishing on the round four-sphere","kind":"A","category":"quantum-field-theory-mathematics","library":"mathematics","order":967.25,"companion":"qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing-on-the-round-four-sphere-examples","requires":["relations-functions-and-quotients","compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives","grothendieck-spectral-sequences-and-computations","cohomology-of-quasi-coherent-sheaves-on-affine-and-projective-schemes"],"items":[{"id":"thm-qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing","kind":"theorem","domain":"mathematics","library":"mathematics","title":"Coupled Penrose vanishing on the round four-sphere","reference":"items/thm-qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing.md#Statement","deps":["def-axiom-of-choice","def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles","thm-first-hypercohomology-spectral-sequence","thm-cohomology-projective-space-twisting-sheaves"],"dependency_roles":{"def-axiom-of-choice":"mathematical-premise","def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles":"mathematical-premise","thm-first-hypercohomology-spectral-sequence":"mathematical-premise","thm-cohomology-projective-space-twisting-sheaves":"mathematical-premise"},"statement":"Assume AC. Let S4 have positive stereographic orientation for z1=x0+ix1,z2=x2+ix3 and round metric. Let E be any smooth finite-rank Hermitian bundle with smooth unitary ASD connection A. On CP3 use the incidence μ1=z1λ1−bar(z2)λ2, μ2=z2λ1+bar(z1)λ2 and infinity λ=0. Suppose a holomorphic bundle F is smoothly identified with π*E and its Dolbeault operator is the vertical ordinary derivative and the A-horizontal alpha-plane operator. Then H1(CP3,F(-2))=H1(CP3,F∨(-2))=0. Include arbitrary reducible and flat summands. No GAGA, monad or inverse ADHM normal form is assumed.","strategy":"Complete the explicit obligations in dependency order; no source invocation or conditional declaration is a proof.","proof_strategy":"direct","axiom_base":"ZF + full AC inherited through named sheaf/cohomology and matrix suppliers; exact uses must be recorded.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-supplied"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Simon K. Donaldson, The ADHM construction of Yang–Mills instantons","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.08639","locator":"Sections3–6, printedpp4–11, actually read; roadmap invokes Penrose and real normal forms and is not a complete proof of these proposed suppliers."}]},"proof_contract_plan":{"state":"Unproved local established-theory authoring obligation","obligations":["Construct the actual coupled relative Dolbeault/de Rham correspondence complex on the double fibration, with defined sheaves, differentials, domains and resolutions.","Prove local/fiber exactness and the global spectral-sequence edge map, including injectivity rather than merely writing a fiber contour integral.","Prove overlap, global smoothness and gauge/dual naturality of the transform on S4.","Derive the full coupled conformal Laplacian/Weitzenböck formula, scalar coefficient and sign for the stated round scalar-curvature convention; do not copy the source R/8 without verification.","Use compact integration by parts and positivity to prove vanishing for F and F∨, including flat/reducible factors."],"full_statement_not_narrowable_to_evade_obligations":true,"native_authoring_and_review_required":true},"page":"qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing-on-the-round-four-sphere","category":"quantum-field-theory-mathematics","status":"draft","origin":"pipeline","inventory_expansion_required":true,"design_state":"Owner-approved unproved mathematical prerequisite proposal; fresh native supplemental drift and full authoring required.","proof_obligation":"Complete the explicit obligations in dependency order; no source invocation or conditional declaration is a proof.","dependency_level":1}],"status":"draft","scaffold":true,"canonical_scaffold":true}
