+The item dependencies remain `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-holomorphic-germs-at-a-point-form-a-local-ring`, `thm-power-series-expansion-in-several-complex-variables`, `thm-holomorphic-germ-ring-is-noetherian`, `thm-hilbert-basis-theorem`, `thm-noetherian-ring-quotients-and-localisations`, `thm-completion-of-a-noetherian-local-ring`, `thm-flatness-of-noetherian-completion`, `thm-flatness-criteria-by-injections-and-ideals`, `thm-faithfully-flat-ring-map-characterisations`, and `thm-long-exact-tor-sequence-in-the-right-module-variable`. I read Serre, “Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique,” §6 Proposition 3 and Corollary 1, pp. 9–11, and Annex §§21–24, especially Propositions 22–23 and 27–29, pp. 34–40, [source](https://www.college-de-france.fr/media/jean-pierre-serre/UPL1698785858825941763_Serre_GAGA.pdf). The source proves the local completion comparison and flat-pair criteria. Its passage to finite-type nonreduced schemes must use the same finitely generated defining ideal on both sides; the plan correctly keeps that quotient argument and nilpotent retention as local proof obligations rather than treating Serre's classical variety statement as sufficient.
+
+VERDICT: drift-applied — added schemes-subschemes-and-morphisms-locally-of-finite-type (order 892); the finite-type scheme and local-ring hypotheses lacked their exact published definitions in the closure.
+
+### qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity
+
+Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-local-coherent-polydisc-acyclicity`, planned order 967.17. Its direct dependencies are `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence`, `thm-dolbeault-lemma-polydisc`, `thm-dolbeault-cohomology-polydisc-vanishes-positive-q`, `thm-smooth-function-module-sheaves-are-acyclic`, `thm-acyclic-resolution-theorem-for-right-derived-functors`, `thm-long-exact-sequence-sheaf-cohomology`, and `thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise`; each is in the current closure. The statement is local on a neighborhood in `C^N`, so it does not need a separate global complex-manifold supplier.
+
+I read Demailly IX §4.B, (4.3)–Lemma 4.4, p. 421, [source](https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf). Demailly constructs local free resolutions of arbitrary length and shifts cohomology along them on distinguished patches. His stated vanishing range does not, by itself, give every positive degree on a 1-complete polydisc. The proposed proof accounts for this: it separately proves scalar Dolbeault vanishing and the ordinary `2N` cohomological-dimension bound for arbitrary abelian sheaves, then dimension-shifts along the partial resolution. This is a substantial internal proof obligation, but its named suppliers are already present and the claim does not silently rely on global Cartan A/B.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-gaga-compact-coherent-finiteness
+
+Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-compact-projective-coherent-finiteness`, planned order 967.18. Its direct dependencies are `def-axiom-of-choice`, the Oka coherence and local acyclicity items, Artin–Rees and Krull, Cauchy estimates, locally uniform limits of holomorphic functions, Arzelà–Ascoli, Leray/C̆ech comparison, and pseudoconvex Dolbeault vanishing; the declared closure contains their homes. The transitive closure through `qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity` also contains `divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality`, which houses the published definition of (mathbb P^r(mathbb C)) as a compact complex manifold with its standard charts. No additional prerequisite edge is needed.
+
+I read Demailly IX §1 (including Theorem 1.9), §4.C–4.D (including Proposition 4.7 and Theorem 4.8), pp. 406–407 and 421–424, in the same [source](https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf). The Cartan–Serre proof uses coherent-section Fréchet topologies, compact restriction maps, acyclic covers, and the Schwartz compact-complex finiteness theorem. The item contract explicitly retains Fréchet open mapping, the Schwartz result, chart-independent coherent-section topology, several-variable Montel, compact restriction, and finite coherent-acyclic cover constructions as proof work. These are not accepted merely by citing Demailly; no missing existing supplier page was identified.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-gaga-projective-scalar-dolbeault
+
+Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology`, planned order 967.19. The statement quantifies over every holomorphic vector bundle on (mathbb P^r(mathbb C)). The existing `divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality` requirement already supplies the published projective-space definition, but the closure lacked the exact holomorphic-vector-bundle definition. I added `compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives` (order 1797), home of `def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles`. The item's proof suppliers are otherwise present; the pseudoconvex Dolbeault supplier was also absent from the original closure, so I added `hormander-estimates-and-the-levi-problem` (order 1624), home of `cor-dolbeault-vanishing-pseudoconvex-domain`.
+
+The direct item dependencies are `def-axiom-of-choice`, the polydisc Dolbeault lemma and vanishing, smooth-module acyclicity, the acyclic-resolution theorem, polydisc Cauchy and annular Laurent results, holomorphic dependence of Laurent coefficients, locally uniform limits, Leray/C̆ech comparison, and pseudoconvex Dolbeault vanishing. I read Serre §13 Lemma 4 and footnote 4, pp. 20–21, and Demailly VII §10.6–10.7, pp. 348–349. Serre proves the structure-sheaf comparison by algebraic vanishing and Dolbeault theory; his footnote says the alternative Laurent calculation was an unpublished Frenkel computation. Demailly's cited projective argument uses Hodge theory, duality, and Nakano vanishing, which the proposed statement excludes. The direct proof obligation on (mathbb C^a\times(mathbb C^\times)^b) cover intersections, parameter holomorphy, normal convergence, and the sign-correct Laurent Čech contraction is therefore necessary and remains open for authoring.
+
+VERDICT: drift-applied — added hormander-estimates-and-the-levi-problem (order 1624), compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives (order 1797); the pseudoconvex scalar-vanishing supplier and exact bundle definition were missing from the closure.
+
+### qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing-on-the-round-four-sphere
+
+Item: `thm-qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing`, planned order 967.25. The existing closure includes the complex-manifold/bundle, Hodge, hypercohomology, and projective-scheme cohomology suppliers, but it lacked the exact analytic definition of (mathbb{CP}^3) used by the incidence coordinates and line restrictions. I added `divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality` (order 1612), whose published `def-complex-projective-space-and-holomorphic-charts` defines (mathbb P^n(mathbb C)) as the space of complex lines with its quotient topology and standard holomorphic charts.
+
+I read Donaldson, “The ADHM construction of Yang–Mills instantons,” §§3–6, pp. 4–11, [source](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.08639), and the primary source Hitchin, “Linear field-equations on self-dual spaces,” §3 Theorem 3.1 and Corollary 3.8, pp. 181–186, [source](https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1980.0028). Hitchin proves the Penrose map from (H^1(Z,mathcal O_F(-m-2))) to solutions of the corresponding field equation for a self-dual space and a self-dual connection; for compact positive-scalar-curvature (X) and unitary (E), Corollary 3.8 gives vanishing. This is the relevant published result for (m=0), but the current item uses a specifically oriented anti-self-dual convention and explicit incidence operators. The author must prove the orientation/duality identification, the global edge-map injectivity, the dual-bundle case, and the exact round Weitzenböck coefficient/sign. The owner proof contract already preserves these obligations; Donaldson's overview alone is not a proof.
+
+VERDICT: drift-applied — added divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality (order 1612); the exact analytic projective-space definition was missing from the closure.
+
+### qftx-positive-real-linear-monad-normal-forms
+
+Item: `thm-qftx-positive-real-adhm-monad-normal-form`, planned order 967.26. The closure contains the generic complex-manifold/bundle definition, projective-scheme cohomology, the ADHM matrix definition and finite-dimensional real/complex quotient theorem. It lacked the exact analytic (mathbb{CP}^3) definition for the stated coordinates, (sigma), (mathcal O(pm1)) monad, and real-line incidence. I added `divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality` (order 1612), home of the published projective-space definition; the existing projective twisting-sheaf supplier supplies the (mathcal O(m)) context.
+
+The item dependencies remain `def-axiom-of-choice`, `def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles`, the first hypercohomology spectral sequence, projective twisting-sheaf cohomology, `def-qftx-adhm-linear-data-stability-and-regularity`, and `thm-qftx-adhm-real-complex-quotient-correspondence`. I read Donaldson §§3–6, pp. 4–11, [source](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.08639). It supplies Ward/monad context and the standard matrix construction, but it does not prove the proposed intrinsic positive (sigma)-Hermitian normalization, positivity of internal forms, residual (U(k)) uniqueness, inverse extraction, rotation weights, or first-order-family compatibility. Those remain explicit local proof obligations in the proposal; no source-reading limit is being treated as proof coverage, and no old-page dependency or scope change was introduced.
+
+VERDICT: drift-applied — added divisors-riemann-roch-and-duality (order 1612); the exact analytic projective-space definition was missing from the closure.
