Role: alpha / supplemental prerequisite review 2  
Scope: the seven assigned new A pages only.

I compared each assigned theorem's exact statement, item dependencies, and proof-contract hypotheses with its declared page closure and the supplied source/design records. The candidate lists in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-append-2-drift-evidence.json` were treated as reading leads, not as findings. I added six existing published prerequisite-page edges to the seven new A rows; no item statement, scope, order, manifest, or content carrier was changed. I ran the assigned `validate-plan` command after each row edit. The first pass exposed the pseudoconvex-domain supplier edge recorded below; all later passes returned `OK` with only the plan's existing redundant-prerequisite warnings.

### qftx-gaga-analytic-coherence

Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence`, planned order 967.15. The statement is on every finite-dimensional complex manifold `M` and uses its holomorphic structure sheaf `O_M`; the original closure supplied local holomorphic-germ, Weierstrass, noetherian finite-presentation, and stalkwise exactness results, but did not supply the manifold and structure-sheaf definition. I added `compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives` (order 1797), the canonical home of published `def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles`. That definition gives the complex manifold atlas and defines `O_M` as the sheaf of holomorphic germs. The added page edge is for this definition; the item has no Hodge-theory supplier in its item-level `deps`.

The remaining declared item dependencies are `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-holomorphic-germ-ring-is-noetherian`, `thm-weierstrass-preparation-theorem`, `thm-weierstrass-division-theorem`, `lem-generic-linear-coordinate-makes-a-holomorphic-germ-regular`, `thm-finite-generation-and-finite-presentation-over-a-noetherian-ring`, and `thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise`; their homes are already in the closure. I read Demailly, *Complex Analytic and Differential Geometry*, II §3.3, Theorem 3.19 and Lemma 3.20, pp. 89–90, [source](https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf). The proof uses dimension induction, Weierstrass preparation/division, and generators uniform on one neighborhood. The plan correctly retains local coherent-kernel calculus and finite partial resolutions as authoring obligations; the source does not supply a global free resolution.

VERDICT: drift-applied — added compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives (order 1797); the exact complex-manifold and structure-sheaf definition was absent from the closure.

### qftx-gaga-local-analytic-flatness

Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-local-ring-flatness`, planned order 967.16. Its hypotheses quantify over a finite-type complex scheme `X` and a complex closed point `x`, and its conclusion compares the algebraic and analytic local rings at `x`. The original closure had the analytic local-ring, power-series, completion, noetherian, flatness, faithful-flatness, and Tor suppliers, but lacked the scheme and finite-type-morphism definitions. I added `schemes-subschemes-and-morphisms-locally-of-finite-type` (order 892). Its published `def-locally-finite-type-and-finite-type-morphism`, together with the page's affine-scheme and structure-sheaf prerequisites, supplies the finite-type scheme and local-ring context.

The item dependencies remain `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-holomorphic-germs-at-a-point-form-a-local-ring`, `thm-power-series-expansion-in-several-complex-variables`, `thm-holomorphic-germ-ring-is-noetherian`, `thm-hilbert-basis-theorem`, `thm-noetherian-ring-quotients-and-localisations`, `thm-completion-of-a-noetherian-local-ring`, `thm-flatness-of-noetherian-completion`, `thm-flatness-criteria-by-injections-and-ideals`, `thm-faithfully-flat-ring-map-characterisations`, and `thm-long-exact-tor-sequence-in-the-right-module-variable`. I read Serre, “Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique,” §6 Proposition 3 and Corollary 1, pp. 9–11, and Annex §§21–24, especially Propositions 22–23 and 27–29, pp. 34–40, [source](https://www.college-de-france.fr/media/jean-pierre-serre/UPL1698785858825941763_Serre_GAGA.pdf). The source proves the local completion comparison and flat-pair criteria. Its passage to finite-type nonreduced schemes must use the same finitely generated defining ideal on both sides; the plan correctly keeps that quotient argument and nilpotent retention as local proof obligations rather than treating Serre's classical variety statement as sufficient.

VERDICT: drift-applied — added schemes-subschemes-and-morphisms-locally-of-finite-type (order 892); the finite-type scheme and local-ring hypotheses lacked their exact published definitions in the closure.

### qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity

Item: `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-local-coherent-polydisc-acyclicity`, planned order 967.17. Its direct dependencies are `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence`, `thm-dolbeault-lemma-polydisc`, `thm-dolbeault-cohomology-polydisc-vanishes-positive-q`, `thm-smooth-function-module-sheaves-are-acyclic`, `thm-acyclic-resolution-theorem-for-right-derived-functors`, `thm-long-exact-sequence-sheaf-cohomology`, and `thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise`; each is in the current closure. The statement is local on a neighborhood in `C^N`, so it does not need a separate global complex-manifold supplier.

I read Demailly IX §4.B, (4.3)–Lemma 4.4, p. 421, [source](https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf). Demailly constructs local free resolutions of arbitrary length and shifts cohomology along them on distinguished patches. His stated vanishing range does not, by itself, give every positive degree on a 1-complete polydisc. The proposed proof accounts for this: it separately proves scalar Dolbeault vanishing and the ordinary `2N` cohomological-dimension bound for arbitrary abelian sheaves, then dimension-shifts along the partial resolution. This is a substantial internal proof obligation, but its named suppliers are already present and the claim does not silently rely on global Cartan A/B.

