+            "thm-continuous-dependence-of-odes-on-initial-data-and-parameters": "mathematical-premise"
+          },
+          "statement": "For the compact connected base and regularity above, evaluation identifies the stabilizer at A with the centralizer of Hol_A in SU(N); irreducible A has stabilizer Z_N. If A_j→A and A_j^{u_j}→B in H^k, then a subsequence u_j converges in H^{k+1}. Consequently the action of Gbar_{k+1} on A_k^* is free and proper.",
+          "strategy": "Use parallel-transport ODE and compactness at one fibre for a uniform-convergent subsequence, then bootstrap d u=u B-A u in Sobolev norms. Supply finite-atlas proof for arbitrary smooth P/SU(N), not merely cite NR S3/SU2. Apply the inspected complex-unitary Schur statement to the holonomy representation, whose operators are bounded in finite dimension; determinant one reduces unit scalars to Z_N.",
