+          "proof_obligation": "Generalize the written curve Dolbeault resolution pattern directly in all dimensions ≤3 using local polydisc exactness and smooth-module acyclicity. In the standard projective cover identify finite intersections with products of C and C*, prove scalar acyclicity using explicit pseudoconvex exhaustions and scalar Dolbeault solvability (or direct Laurent solution). Expand holomorphic functions on polyannuli, prove parameter holomorphy, normal convergence and uniqueness by iterated Cauchy integrals. Decompose homogeneous degree-zero Laurent modes and give a sign-correct Čech contracting homotopy for positive degree, verifying subseries extend to the claimed charts and converge locally uniformly. Global degree-zero functions are constants. This source-guided Laurent reconstruction is not supplied by the algebraic O(m) theorem and not proved by Serre’s footnote. For the standard projective cover, intersections are C^a times (C*)^b, not polydiscs. Prove their required scalar acyclicity by an explicit annular-product Dolbeault/exhaustion or Laurent argument before using Leray; local coherent acyclicity alone does not imply it."
